Tax Treaties
As above mentioned, according to the Sino-U.S. Tax Treaty which was effective on January 1st, 1987 and aimed to avoid double
taxation disadvantage, income that is incurred in one nation should be taxed by that nation and exempted from the other nation, but for the
dividend that is generated in China and distributed to foreigners in other nations, a rate 10% tax will be charged.
